<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uzbekistan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uzbekistan is a country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> covering much of historic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a>, including the cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a>. It was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>, whose capital was Samarkand, and an important part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Empire</a>. Many of the region's great medieval monuments date from the Timurid period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uzbekistan.jpg" alt="Uzbekistan" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Farhod Yoʻldoshev · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Uzbekistan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
